{
  "id": "r01",
  "text": "Imagine deleting a free game because your console needs the space. Usually, that's a boring decision. You open your library later, download it again, and carry on. With P.T., that ordinary expectation broke. This is a real PlayStation Four download error from GameSpot's test in May twenty fifteen. The game wasn't just missing from the shop. Even somebody who had downloaded it before could find that the route back no longer worked. Meanwhile, another console could still have a playable installation. Same game, different outcome, depending on what was already on the drive. That's the strange afterlife of P.T.: a horror teaser that made people afraid of a storage decision. To understand why anybody cared this much about a free download, we need to go back to the room it put you in.",
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
